From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:38:21 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 41/72] deepseek: stage and send grammar masks only where a row
 is constrained

Every target window and prompt staged its grammar rows through Masks.stage,
even with none: rank 0 then sent an op_grammar plan frame to the TP peer on
every forward of every request, and rows that allow every token (a thinking
prefix, forced rows past a rejection) were copied, shipped whole over the plan
link, uploaded and masked to no effect. Such rows are now dropped, and a stage
with nothing to apply and nothing applied before returns at once; a stage that
clears earlier masks still reaches the followers.
